<title>USA: Commercial Federal Corp Q1 Sept 30 loss.</title>
<headline>Commercial Federal Corp Q1 Sept 30 loss.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Neb. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.27   profit	 $0.77</p>
<p> Net loss		   4,050   profit	11,244</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,743		   15,283</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>Assets $6.67 billion vs $6.61 billion</p>
<p>Deposits $4.27 billion vs $4.30 billion</p>
<p>Loans receivable $4.77 billion vs $4.72 billion  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q1 results include charge for Savings Association Insurance Fund recapitalization of $17.3 million or $1.17/shr (after tax). Also included are a charge of $1.5 million or $0.10/shr for transaction costs for repurchase of 1.3 million shares and a nonrecurring charge of $103,000 or $0.01/shr for a tax law change regarding tax bad debt reserves.</p>
<p>1995 Q1 results include charge of $1.2 million or $0.09/shr for expenses associated with the purchase of Railroad Financial Corp.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
